# Python Rules (PEP 8)

- Follow PEP 8 for layout, naming, imports, and whitespace.
- Use 4 spaces per indentation level; never use tabs.
- Keep line length <= 88 characters (prefer wrapping before this when readability improves).
- Use `snake_case` for functions/variables, `PascalCase` for classes, `UPPER_CASE` for constants.
- Group imports as stdlib, third-party, then local; separate groups with one blank line.
- Add docstrings for public modules, classes, and functions.
- Catch specific exceptions when practical; avoid bare `except`.
- Keep functions focused and short; extract helpers for repeated or complex logic.
- Prefer type hints for new/changed public interfaces.
- Before finalizing Python edits, run a style check (`pycodestyle`) and fix violations in touched files.
